  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 46 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, a person who instigates another to commit an offence, such as theft, is guilty of abetting that offence. Specifically, if a person (A) intends to cause theft and encourages another person (B) to take property belonging to someone else, A is guilty of abetting theft, even if B does not commit the theft due to a misunderstanding about the ownership of the property. This is illustrated in Section 46 Illustration(d), where A instigates B to take property, leading to A being liable for abetting theft.",
